Note on dependencies

cli-zapp links against go.mau.fi/whatsmeow, which is licensed MPL-2.0.
MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: using it does not require this project's own
source to be released under the MPL, which is why cli-zapp can be MIT.

Any file derived from whatsmeow remains under MPL-2.0. cli-zapp does not
vendor or modify whatsmeow; it imports it as a module dependency, so the
obligation is satisfied by the module boundary itself.

